*.md whitespace=-trailing-space,-blank-at-eol

# WHY `-merge` on these five: each is a whole-file artifact derived from the
# krites source tree, so any two branches that touch the crate conflict in all
# of them regardless of whether their code overlaps (aletheia#6653 -- merging
# one wave immediately turned the other four dirty). `-merge` tells git to take
# our side wholesale and declare the conflict, rather than interleaving conflict
# markers into a file whose only correct resolution is to recompute it.
#
# That matters beyond convenience: regenerating against a ledger that still
# carries conflict markers cannot parse it, and the regenerator used to treat an
# unparsable prior ledger as "nothing to preserve" -- silently rewriting every
# dual/sovereign row as `derived` with its soak window zeroed (aletheia#6703).
# Never producing markers removes the trap rather than guarding it twice.
#
# Resolution is therefore: merge, run scripts/regen-krites-artifacts.sh, stage.
# The gate is the backstop -- check-krites-provenance.py and the three
# module-dag --check invocations all fail on a stale artifact, so forgetting the
# regenerate step is loud rather than silent.
#
# CAPABILITY_MATRIX.toml is deliberately absent: it is hand-maintained and only
# checked, never generated, so a conflict there needs a human, not a recompute.
crates/krites/PROVENANCE.toml            -merge
crates/krites/NOTICE.md                  -merge
crates/krites/module-dag.json            -merge
crates/krites/module-dag.md              -merge
crates/krites/module-dag.wave-scope.json -merge
